{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:30)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:30)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> denote the smallest positive integer that is divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/1288f16f77606bb83db76df0877615ef6e8b149e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> and whose base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> representation consists of only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s, with at least one of each. What are the last four digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28578f91569670ce8f5d1c27b4ea637a09a75a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e899090e32e4888e3a6386d0086d42c6c1ca15bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 4444 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 4494 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 4944 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 9444 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 9944$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"489\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a number to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4054552638cf9f29e857a1306bd3ec31df3c19b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> the last two digits have to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> That means the last two digits of this integer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb15a16cca90d201094265ee529e9e2cfb113de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>For a number to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/8/1288f16f77606bb83db76df0877615ef6e8b149e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> the sum of all the digits must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> The way to make this happen most efficiently is with nine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s - if we add nines, we preserve the residue of the sum modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, we also need one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The smallest integer that meets all these conditions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3d9315f52aad60db88b49b77dd9ded12d35cae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4444444944$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />. The last four digits are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d33a136bc14c6622fc9884bf58dc97b150a8e66b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } 4944}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"81\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:30.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:30)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:30)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:30)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/k273aq44mXU\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/k273aq44mXU</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is covered 1:00-2:30\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p5f1u44-pvQ?t=59\">https://youtu.be/p5f1u44-pvQ?t=59</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table c